WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:10.759
The landscape gizmo brush is one of the other tools that we can use to modify or affect our landscapes look and feel.

2
00:00:10.759 --> 00:00:17.760
Unlike the brush tools, this one allows us to do the following.

3
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:24.260
We can either copy existing parts of our landscape and then paste them to other locations in our landscape.

4
00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:30.260
Or for our example what we're going to do is we're actually going to use this tool to import a height map

5
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:37.259
and then use the gizmo to place where inside of our landscape that height map should affect.

6
00:00:37.259 --> 00:00:47.259
Now one of the advantages of doing it this way is that the gizmo import export supports the R16 height map option.

7
00:00:47.259 --> 00:00:53.259
The reason this is so beneficial is that when you're using the R16 height map format,

8
00:00:53.259 --> 00:01:00.259
you're going to greatly reduce the amount of artifacts or stair stepping patterns that you see inside of the landscape.

9
00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:07.260
Now these stair stepping artifacts are easy to fix, but they can be a little annoying, especially as you're crafting your landscape.

10
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:15.299
So for us, what we're going to do as soon as we select our height map, we then need to change our height map size.

11
00:01:15.299 --> 00:01:18.299
And this is going to be based off of the size of the texture.

12
00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:22.299
So for our example, our texture is going to be 2048 by 2048.

13
00:01:22.299 --> 00:01:28.299
So we're going to put that number in. And then once we hit import, we're going to get something that looks like this.

14
00:01:28.299 --> 00:01:35.299
The gizmo brush will reflect the look of the texture that we've used to import as our height map.

15
00:01:35.299 --> 00:01:43.299
And then we can go through our level and add this content to our landscape wherever we want,

16
00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:51.299
by either utilizing the brush to paint it in or by pressing control V on the keyboard to paste things into our landscape.

17
00:01:51.299 --> 00:01:52.299
So let's go ahead and look at that now.

18
00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:57.299
So we're going to come over here, make sure we have our landscape and our sculpt, and I'm going to come to our copy.

19
00:01:57.299 --> 00:02:00.390
And generally it looks like this.

20
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.390
So we're going to come down here to our advanced.

21
00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.390
We're going to make sure gizmo import export.

22
00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.389
We're going to select our height map, which is in this case going to be our impact crater.

23
00:02:08.389 --> 00:02:09.389
So I'm going to hit open.

24
00:02:09.389 --> 00:02:12.389
We know our size here is going to be 2048 by 2048.

25
00:02:12.389 --> 00:02:13.389
So that's good.

26
00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:15.389
And there's our gizmo right there.

27
00:02:15.389 --> 00:02:18.389
So let's go ahead and hit import and give this just a moment to update.

28
00:02:18.389 --> 00:02:20.389
And that is what it looks like. There we go.

29
00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:22.389
So let's go ahead and hit control V right now.

30
00:02:22.389 --> 00:02:25.389
And let's just look at G to see what this does.

31
00:02:25.389 --> 00:02:26.389
So there it is.

32
00:02:26.389 --> 00:02:29.389
It is doing it kind of in a circle here.

33
00:02:29.389 --> 00:02:33.389
So there's a couple of ways that we could get rid of that.

34
00:02:33.389 --> 00:02:41.389
We could turn off this use smooth gizmo brush to kind of get all the way into the edges there.

35
00:02:41.389 --> 00:02:46.389
The other thing that we can do, too, is this is going to be directly related to the height.

36
00:02:46.389 --> 00:02:57.550
So as I kind of sink this down into our landscape, you can see here it has made some really great little craters in this area.

37
00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:01.550
And then if I was to kind of bring this up, maybe move it over here.

38
00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:04.550
Let me just get out of the way and kind of bring this all the way up.

39
00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:11.550
You're going to see I'll hit control V and it's going to actually raise kind of everything up to meet that area right there.

40
00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:20.030
So just keep that in mind that when you're using this tool, the location of this matters the most.

41
00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:25.030
And we can also affect things in both the positive and the negative.

42
00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:31.030
One of the other things is if we change this pace mode, for example, if I hit this just to like lower and hit control V,

43
00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:38.030
it's going to push everything down for me. But I do need to make sure that I am relatively close

44
00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:44.030
or protruding inside of the height map here to get that to work very well.

45
00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.030
So if I was to do the raise something similar, it's going to raise this stuff up.

46
00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.030
So there we go. Just raised everything.

47
00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.030
Probably going to bring this up just a little bit more to get some more stuff raised up.

48
00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.030
So there we go. So that looks actually looks kind of cool there on the side of the mountain.

49
00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:07.030
So what I want everybody to do now is just spend the next few minutes taking this landscape gizmo and adjusting it.

50
00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:11.030
We can move it around. We can also rotate it and we can also scale it.

51
00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:15.030
So spend some time just adjusting this and scaling it and playing with the values.

52
00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:20.029
And we'll see you in just a little bit with the next part in our tutorial.
